From: The Omarchy Authors <dev@omarchy.org>
Subject: [PATCH] platform: gate and harden experimental GB10 CX7 power control

Keep the ACPI driver unbound without an explicit experimental opt-in.
Move GPIO handling entirely to threaded IRQ context. Serialize the two
GPIO threads and sysfs transitions before taking the PCI rescan/remove
lock; the PCI notifier never acquires the transition mutex. Drain sysfs,
then IRQs and notifier callbacks, before releasing hardware references.

Validate firmware fields before shifts and MMIO accesses, propagate mapping
failures, and balance device/runtime-PM references. This does not supply the
userspace endpoint removal/rescan coordinator or qualify physical power
transitions. Carry the changes separately from the pinned NVIDIA source.

